  "notes": "Removing pay_status costs 0.04719 ROC-AUC, the largest leave-one-out loss, against a fold-SD of 0.00712. pay_status alone reaches 0.74915 versus 0.78454 for the full feature set, so it carries most of the available signal on its own. This confirms the Phase 1 conclusion that repayment status dominates the monetary columns. Leave-one-out and only-one disagree in the usual way: a group can be individually predictive yet redundant once the others are present, which is exactly what collinear BILL_AMT columns produce. Both views are reported rather than one. Dropping the demographic group costs +0.00132 ROC-AUC; the drop_demographic arm is consumed by WP17, which tests whether the financial columns proxy for the removed demographics (Barocas & Selbst, 2016)."
